1 Persons and entities that accept deposits and grant loans on a professional basis are prohibited from accepting deposits from the following persons, organisations or entities where the total value of the deposits per person, organisation or entity exceeds 100 000 francs:
a. Russian nationals;
b. natural persons resident in the Russian Federation;
c. banks, enterprises or organisations established in the Russian Federation;
d. banks, enterprises or organisations established outside Switzerland or the EEA whose shares are more than fifty per cent held, directly or indirectly, by Russian nationals or by natural persons resident in the Russian Federation.²⁸⁶

2 The direct or indirect provision, on a professional basis, of the following services to Russian nationals, natural persons resident in the Russian Federation or legal entities, enterprises or organisations established in the Russian Federation is prohibited:
a. crypto services;
b. issuing payment instruments, acquiring and settling payment transactions, or payment initiation;
c. issuing e-money.²⁸⁷

2bis It is prohibited to make the following possible for Russian nationals or natural persons resident in the Russian Federation:
a.²⁸⁸ the acquisition of direct or indirect ownership of legal entities, enterprises or organisations founded or registered under the law of Switzerland or of an EEA member state that provide crypto services;
b. direct or indirect control over legal entities, enterprises or organisations under letter a;
c. the exercise of a function in the management bodies of legal entities, enterprises or organisations under letter a.²⁸⁹

3 The prohibitions under paragraphs 1–2bis do not apply to Swiss nationals, nationals of an EEA member state or of the United Kingdom, or natural persons holding a temporary or permanent residence permit of Switzerland, of an EEA member state or of the United Kingdom.²⁹⁰

3bis The prohibitions under paragraph 2 letters b and c do not apply to the provision of personalised security features necessary for access to an account with a financial institution or e-money institution in Switzerland, an EEA member state or a partner.²⁹¹

4 After consulting the competent units of the EDA and the EFD, SECO may authorise exceptions to the prohibitions under paragraphs 1 and 2 for deposits or services that are necessary for:
a. avoiding cases of hardship;
b. humanitarian or evacuation purposes;
c. civil society activities that directly promote democracy, human rights or the rule of law in the Russian Federation;
d. the payment of fees or charges for the routine holding or maintenance of frozen funds or economic resources;
e. the performance of official activities of diplomatic or consular missions or of international organisations;
f. safeguarding Swiss interests;
g. non-prohibited cross-border trade in goods and services between Switzerland and the Russian Federation, between Switzerland and the EEA, or between the EEA and the Russian Federation;
h. the restructuring or liquidation of a legal entity connected with the organisation listed in Annex 8 under SSID number 175-54340.²⁹²

5 After consulting the competent units of the EDA and the EFD, it may authorise exceptions to the prohibitions under paragraph 2 letters b and c for services intended for the exclusive use of legal entities, enterprises or organisations in the Russian Federation that are owned or solely or jointly controlled by legal entities, enterprises or organisations founded or registered under Swiss law, the law of an EEA member state or the law of a partner.²⁹³

