1 Persons and entities that accept deposits and grant loans on a professional basis are prohibited from accepting deposits from the following persons, organisations or entities where the total value of the deposits per person, organisation or entity exceeds 100 000 francs:
a. Belarusian nationals;
b. natural persons resident in Belarus;
c. banks, enterprises and organisations established in Belarus;
d. banks, enterprises or organisations established outside Switzerland or the EEA whose shares are more than 50 per cent held, directly or indirectly, by Belarusian nationals or by natural persons resident in Belarus.⁹¹

1bis The direct or indirect provision, on a professional basis, of the following services to Belarusian nationals, natural persons resident in Belarus or legal entities, enterprises or organisations established in Belarus is prohibited:
a. crypto services;
b. issuing payment instruments, acquiring and settling payment transactions, or payment initiation;
c. issuing e-money.⁹²

1ter It is prohibited to make the following possible for Belarusian nationals or natural persons resident in Belarus:
a.⁹³ the acquisition of direct or indirect ownership of legal entities, enterprises or organisations founded or registered under the law of Switzerland or of an EEA member state that provide crypto services;
b. direct or indirect control over legal entities, enterprises or organisations under letter a;
c. the exercise of a function in the management bodies of legal entities, enterprises or organisations under letter a.⁹⁴

2 The prohibitions under paragraphs 1–1ter do not apply to Swiss nationals, nationals of an EEA member state or of the United Kingdom, or natural persons holding a temporary or permanent residence permit of Switzerland, of an EEA member state or of the United Kingdom.⁹⁵

2bis The prohibitions under paragraph 1bis letters b and c do not apply to the provision of personalised security features necessary for access to an account with a financial institution or e-money institution in Switzerland, an EEA member state or a partner.⁹⁶

3 After consulting the competent units of the EDA and the EFD, SECO may authorise exceptions to the prohibitions under paragraphs 1 and 1bis for deposits or services that are necessary for:
a. avoiding cases of hardship;
b. humanitarian or evacuation purposes;
c. civil society activities that directly promote democracy, human rights or the rule of law in Belarus;
d. the payment of fees or charges for the routine holding or maintenance of frozen funds or economic resources;
e. the performance of official activities of diplomatic or consular missions or of international organisations;
f. safeguarding Swiss interests;
g. non-prohibited cross-border trade in goods and services between Switzerland and Belarus, between Switzerland and the EEA, or between the EEA and Belarus.⁹⁷

4 After consulting the competent units of the EDA and the EFD, SECO may authorise exceptions to the prohibitions under paragraph 1bis letters b and c for services intended for the exclusive use of legal entities, enterprises or organisations in Belarus that are owned or solely or jointly controlled by legal entities, enterprises or organisations founded or registered under Swiss law, the law of an EEA member state or the law of a partner.⁹⁸

⁹¹ Amended by No. I of the Ordinance of 14 May 2025, in force since 1 June 2025 (AS 2025 316).

⁹² Inserted by No. I of the Ordinance of 14 May 2025 (AS 2025 316). Amended by No. I of the Ordinance of 25 Feb. 2026, in force since 26 Feb. 2026 (AS 2026 91).

⁹³ Amended by No. I of the Ordinance of 4 Nov. 2026, in force since 5 Nov. 2026 (AS 2026 600).

